om the rollback tool. After each attempt I checked status: all regions are still on v2.3.1 and the service is still unhealthy. On-call needs to finish the rollback to v2.3.0 by hand, or once the rollback tool is working again.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-failure"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I couldn't roll checkout-api back. The incident is open, and on-call has been paged.\n\n- **Current state:** v2.3.1 is running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It's failing health checks with an 18% error rate. The release candidate for v2.3.1 also failed health checks in staging.\n- **Target version:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production.\n- **Rollback:** I tried twice, and both times the rollback tool returned a \"503 Service Unavailable\" error. After each attempt I checked the service status: nothing changed, and every region is still on the failing v2.3.1.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open as a SEV2 for checkout-api and paged on-call. It says what's failing, what I tried and that the rollback to v2.3.0 still needs to be done.\n\nAnother way to get back to v2.3.0 would be the regular deploy tool. That version was healthy in production, so it doesn't need change-manager approval. I didn't do this because you asked for a rollback, and switching to a different method in production should be your call. If you'd like me to deploy v2.3.0, or try the rollback again once the tool is working, just say so.", "type": "text"}]}]}